From: Martin Lepage <ml@pharos-ai.ca>
Subject: [PATCH] fix(backend): restore dnspython==2.6.1 for mongodb+srv:// Atlas resolution

PR #4 slimmed requirements.txt and removed dnspython. This is a latent P1:
Motor/PyMongo resolve mongodb+srv://<cluster>.mongodb.net/<db> connection strings
via DNS SRV lookups, which require the `dnspython` package. Without it, the
AsyncIOMotorClient call raises ConfigurationError at startup and every DB-backed
endpoint 500s — silently in dev (where most devs use mongodb://localhost), loudly
in prod (Atlas is always SRV).

This patch adds dnspython back with a pinned version and a comment explaining
why it must never be removed again. A regression guard in
tests/test_backend_hardening.py will fail CI if someone removes it in the future.

Closes: PR #4 P1 Codex-review finding
---
 backend/requirements.txt | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/backend/requirements.txt b/backend/requirements.txt
--- a/backend/requirements.txt
+++ b/backend/requirements.txt
@@ -1,4 +1,8 @@
 # backend/requirements.txt
+#
+# CRITICAL: dnspython is required for mongodb+srv:// URI resolution.
+# Removing it causes silent runtime failure on all DB-backed endpoints.
+# Do not remove. Do not move to test-only. Production runtime dependency.

 fastapi==0.110.1
 uvicorn[standard]==0.29.0
@@ -7,6 +11,7 @@
 # Database
 motor==3.3.2
 pymongo==4.7.2
+dnspython==2.6.1                 # REQUIRED for mongodb+srv:// SRV resolution (Atlas)

 # Data validation
 pydantic==2.7.1
